    "decision": "ask",
    "citations": [
      {
        "evidence_id": "docs:fragments:v2:cb48967ad96007e2",
        "quote": "Because parallel fragments run concurrently on separate threads during the initial (full-app) run, a few Streamlit commands aren't safe to call from inside them and will raise an error. These include:"
      }
    ],
    "spans": {
      "sources": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "docs:fragments:v2:cb48967ad96007e2",
          "product_version": null,
          "span_id": "src_498246063fc5f50a83691e96",
          "start": 51,
          "end": 251,
          "text": "Because parallel fragments run concurrently on separate threads during the initial (full-app) run, a few Streamlit commands aren't safe to call from inside them and will raise an error. These include:"
        }
      ],
      "messages": [
        {
          "message_index": 0,
          "span_id": "usr_0f9bb1952c922fb83f7a0f9f",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 900,
          "text": "Conditionally created dialog in a fragment stops logically existing after rerun of a fragment while still existing on the website\n\n### Checklist\n\n- [x] I have searched the [existing issues](https://github.com/streamlit/streamlit/issues) for similar issues.\n- [x] I added a very descriptive title to this issue.\n- [x] I have provided sufficient information below to help reproduce this issue.\n\n### Summary\n\nWhen a fragment gets rerun and it has conditionally rendered child dialog (for example guarded by a button being clicked) the dialog will stop being responsive while still existing on the page\n\n### Reproducible Code Example\n\n```Python\nimport streamlit as st\n\n\n@st.dialog(\"Dialog\", dismissible=False)\ndef show_dialog() -> None:\n    if st.button(\"Increment\"):\n        st.session_state[\"clicks\"] = st.session_state.get(\"clicks\", 0) + 1\n    st.write(\"Clicks:\", st.session_state.get(\"clicks\", 0))\n\n\n"
        },
        {
          "message_index": 0,
          "span_id": "usr_c286efa8f3df38235cae6101",
          "start": 900,
          "end": 1800,
          "text": "@st.fragment(run_every=5)\ndef parent_fragment() -> None:\n    st.session_state[\"parent_runs\"] = st.session_state.get(\"parent_runs\", 0) + 1\n    st.write(\"Parent runs:\", st.session_state[\"parent_runs\"])\n    if st.button(\"Open dialog\"):\n        show_dialog()\n\n\nst.write(\"Open the dialog, then wait for the parent fragment's next automatic rerun (every 5 seconds).\")\nparent_fragment()\n```\n\n### Steps To Reproduce\n\n1. Click Open dialog\n2. start clicking increment\n3. after parent reruns the dialog stops being responsive and streamlit will log The fragment with id <id> does not exist anymore - it might have been removed during a preceding full-app rerun.\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\nThe dialog to still be responsive\n\n### Current Behavior\n\nThe dialog stops being responsive\n\n### Is this a regression?\n\n- [x] Yes, this used to work in a previous version.\n\n### Debug info\n\n- Streamlit version: 1.64.0\n- Python "
        },
        {
          "message_index": 0,
          "span_id": "usr_ae45eef23415186c6c2b3b1a",
          "start": 1800,
          "end": 2104,
          "text": "version: Python 3.13.13\n- Operating System: Linux 7.1.4-arch1-1\n- Browser: Firefox\n\n\n### Additional Information\n\nworked when ran with\n```\nuv run --no-project --with streamlit==1.57.0 streamlit run repro.py\n```\nstopped working at\n```\nuv run --no-project --with streamlit==1.58.0 streamlit run repro.py\n```"
        }
      ]
    },
    "draft": {
      "draft_version": "05ed097fc2beb67965735088404a7b0c6712fffb7318a43b834074f644d67e7c",
